Provider abstraction is the key to clean LLD here — we want to swap SendGrid for Mailgun without touching the orchestrator.

```mermaid
classDiagram
    class NotificationController {
        +POST createNotification(req)
        +GET getStatus(id)
    }
    class IdempotencyChecker {
        +checkAndReserve(key) Result
    }
    class NotificationOrchestrator {
        +process(NotificationRequest)
    }
    class PreferenceService {
        +resolveChannels(userId, category, requested) List~Channel~
    }
    class TemplateRenderer {
        +render(templateId, channel, locale, data) Rendered
    }
    class ChannelDispatcher {
        <<interface>>
        +dispatch(ChannelMessage) DispatchResult
        +channel() Channel
    }
    class EmailDispatcher
    class SmsDispatcher
    class PushDispatcher
    class ProviderClient {
        <<interface>>
        +send(ProviderMessage) ProviderResponse
    }
    class SendGridClient
    class MailgunClient
    class TwilioClient
    class FcmClient
    class RateLimiter {
        +tryAcquire(key) boolean
    }
    class RetryScheduler {
        +schedule(dispatchId, attempt, delay)
    }
    class WebhookHandler {
        +handle(provider, payload)
    }

    NotificationController --> IdempotencyChecker
    NotificationController --> NotificationOrchestrator
    NotificationOrchestrator --> PreferenceService
    NotificationOrchestrator --> TemplateRenderer
    NotificationOrchestrator --> ChannelDispatcher
    ChannelDispatcher <|.. EmailDispatcher
    ChannelDispatcher <|.. SmsDispatcher
    ChannelDispatcher <|.. PushDispatcher
    EmailDispatcher --> ProviderClient
    SmsDispatcher --> ProviderClient
    PushDispatcher --> ProviderClient
    ProviderClient <|.. SendGridClient
    ProviderClient <|.. MailgunClient
    ProviderClient <|.. TwilioClient
    ProviderClient <|.. FcmClient
    EmailDispatcher --> RateLimiter
    EmailDispatcher --> RetryScheduler
```

**Key code paths** (only the interesting bodies):

```java
public class NotificationOrchestrator {
    public void process(NotificationRequest req) {
        List<Channel> channels = prefs.resolveChannels(
            req.userId(), req.category(), req.requestedChannels());
        if (channels.isEmpty()) {
            recordSuppressed(req); return;
        }
        for (Channel ch : channels) {
            Rendered content = templateRenderer.render(
                req.templateId(), ch, userLocale(req.userId()), req.templateData());
            ChannelMessage msg = new ChannelMessage(
                req.notificationId(), req.userId(), ch, content);
            persistDispatch(msg);                                     // status=pending
            dispatchTopic(ch).publish(msg);
        }
    }
}

public class EmailDispatcher implements ChannelDispatcher {
    @Override public DispatchResult dispatch(ChannelMessage msg) {
        if (!rateLimiter.tryAcquire("rate:" + provider.name())) {
            retryScheduler.schedule(msg.dispatchId(), 0, Duration.ofSeconds(1));
            return DispatchResult.RATE_LIMITED;
        }
        try {
            ProviderResponse r = provider.send(buildProviderMessage(msg));
            updateDispatch(msg.dispatchId(), Status.SENT, r.providerMessageId());
            return DispatchResult.SENT;
        } catch (RetryableException e) {
            int attempt = incrementAttempt(msg.dispatchId());
            if (attempt > MAX_ATTEMPTS) { sendToDlq(msg); return DispatchResult.DEAD; }
            retryScheduler.schedule(msg.dispatchId(), attempt, backoff(attempt));
            return DispatchResult.RETRYING;
        } catch (NonRetryableException e) {
            updateDispatch(msg.dispatchId(), Status.FAILED, null);
            return DispatchResult.FAILED;
        }
    }

    private Duration backoff(int attempt) {
        long secs = (long) Math.pow(4, attempt);                       // 1, 4, 16, 64, 256, 1024
        return Duration.ofSeconds(Math.min(secs, 1800));               // cap 30min
    }
}
```

Why this shape:

- **`ChannelDispatcher` interface per channel** — each channel has its own retry/rate policy; sharing one base class would obscure them.
- **`ProviderClient` interface inside each dispatcher** — SendGrid/Mailgun are interchangeable for `EmailDispatcher`; the orchestrator never sees provider names.
- **`RetryScheduler` is its own collaborator** — implemented as a delayed Kafka topic or Redis sorted set with due timestamps; testable in isolation.
- **Idempotency happens in `IdempotencyChecker` at the controller boundary** — not the orchestrator, so duplicate POSTs never even enter the pipeline.
